# uhyve 0.10.0 compatibility patch for newer KVM kernels
# (australVM/docs/spectrum_plan.md §5, Task 8.4 / §6 boot-latency row).
#
# Apply against the crates.io source tree:
#   cp -r ~/.cargo/registry/src/*/uhyve-0.10.0 uhyve-patched && chmod -R u+w uhyve-patched
#   cd uhyve-patched && patch -p0 < docs/uhyve-0.10.0-kvm-compat.patch
#   cargo build --release --offline
#
# Three changes, each independently reasoned:
#  1. init(): install vCPU CPUID *before* the long-mode KVM_SET_SREGS.
#     Newer kernels (reproduced on Linux 7.2.9) validate EFER bits
#     against the current CPUID, so 0.10.0's original order gets
#     EINVAL (BackendError(Error(22)) at vm.rs:505) on every boot.
#  2. COM1 (0x3f8-0x3ff) emulation: hermit's serial console polls the
#     UART line-status register; stock uhyve emulates no serial port,
#     so loader images spin forever reading 0x3fd.
#  3. MMIO scan tolerance: reads/writes to the virtio window without a
#     configured virtio device (and other unhandled MMIO addresses)
#     warn instead of panicking the whole VMM — the same "guest might
#     just be scanning" discipline the PCI config path already has.
# The UHYVE_SREGS_DIAG env-gated bisection block (change 1's evidence)
# is included deliberately: it is how the EINVAL was isolated.
--- /home/leo/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/uhyve-0.10.0/src/linux/x86_64/kvm_cpu.rs	2006-07-24 03:21:28.000000000 +0200
+++ /home/leo/Projects/uhyve-0.10.0-patched/src/linux/x86_64/kvm_cpu.rs	2026-10-18 11:45:42.000261198 +0200
